---
description: Database design standards for PostgreSQL.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Database Standards

Database

PostgreSQL

Query layer

sqlc + pgx

Migration

golang-migrate

Approach

Database-first

---

# Naming

Tables

snake_case

Plural

Examples

users

reservations

membership_tiers

reward_redemptions

---

# Columns

snake_case

Examples

created_at

updated_at

deleted_at

customer_id

reservation_date

---

# Primary Key

id

UUID

Never integer auto increment.

UUIDs are generated by the application layer.

---

# Foreign Keys

Always explicit.

Never implicit relationships.

Naming

fk_<table>_<referenced_table>

---

# Timestamps

Every business table:

created_at

updated_at

Type

TIMESTAMPTZ

Timezone

UTC

---

# Soft Delete

Use soft delete only for entities that require recovery or historical retention.

Soft-deletable tables include:

deleted_at

Prefer soft delete for:

users

memberships

menu_items

Avoid soft delete for immutable ledgers:

loyalty_transactions

audit_logs

---

# Audit Fields

When applicable

created_by

updated_by

deleted_by

---

# Indexes

Create indexes only when justified.

Document why.

Naming

idx_<table>_<column>

Unique

uq_<table>_<column>

---

# Constraints

Always define:

Foreign Keys

Unique Constraints

Check Constraints

---

# Transactions

Use transactions when updating multiple entities.

Managed from the Service layer.

---

# Migrations

One logical change per migration.

Never edit an applied migration.

Provide up and down scripts whenever possible.

Filename format

YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.up.sql

YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.down.sql

---

# sqlc

Keep SQL queries under database/queries.

Generate code with sqlc.

Never edit generated code manually.

---

# Seed

Provide seed data for:

Roles

Permissions

Membership Tiers

Reward Types

Settings

Admin User

---

# Goal

Data integrity first.
